INSTALL - install CloverOS
Usage: install [options] [target]
       install <action> [target]

Copies the CloverOS system tree to a target directory, writes the
configuration an installed system needs, creates the first account, and
records a SHA-256 manifest of everything it wrote.

Actions:
  (default)   guided installation
  verify      check installed files against the SHA-256 manifest
  status      print what is installed
  disks       list installation targets
  tasks       list available task sets

Options:
  --local              install from repository files on this computer
  --net                install from GitHub (requires HTTP)
  --local-source <p>   install from an explicit repository root
  --target <path>      install target (default: /)
  --type <mode>        erase, alongside or manual
  --root <path>        manual layout: root mount point
  --home <path>        manual layout: home mount point
  --boot <path>        manual layout: boot mount point
  --erase-data         allow the installer to erase existing data
  --taskset <list>     comma separated task sets
  --user <name>        initial account
  --password <pw>      initial account password (unattended only)
  --hostname <name>    system hostname
  --lang <code>        locale, e.g. en-US
  --session <name>     gnome (default) or text
  --dry-run            show the plan without writing anything
  --no-prompt, -y      never ask; use defaults
  --force              do not ask for confirmation
  --quiet, -q          less output
  --help, -h           show the option list
  --version, -V        print the CloverOS version

Examples:
  install --local --no-prompt
  install /disk --local --taskset fun
  install verify /cloveros
  install status /cloveros
  install tasks

Task sets:
  minimal      text shell only
  terminal     full shell, editors and core tools
  utilities    everyday command line tools
  desktop      the GNOME desktop (CloverOS)
  fun          fortune, cowsay and trains
  development  development extras

Notes:
- What an installation writes:
    etc/fstab                     filesystem table
    etc/clover/mounts.cfg         mount layout
    etc/clover/install.cfg        installation record
    var/lib/install-manifest.sha256   integrity manifest
    var/lib/install-status.txt    status of the last installation
    var/log/install.log           installation log
- `verify` compares every installed file against the manifest and reports
  what is missing or changed.
- An installation of type erase needs --erase-data, or it refuses to run.
- --no-prompt uses defaults for anything not given on the command line.
